From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: R51 Evidence <r51@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:20:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] libc++abi: preserve foreign forced-unwind state
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A foreign exception rethrown through __cxa_rethrow currently starts a new
unwind with _Unwind_RaiseException. For pthread cancellation this loses the
forced-unwind continuation. Use _Unwind_Resume_or_Rethrow for foreign
exceptions while retaining the existing native and SJLJ paths.

On ARM EHABI, the resumed forced unwind may reach a catching handler during
the cleanup phase. Treat a non-zero ttypeIndex as a catching handler and do
not register it through __cxa_begin_cleanup, matching libstdc++'s
found_cleanup gate.

The two changes form one series: applying only the rethrow change exposes the
EHABI cleanup-registration defect on ARM. Validation covers x86_64 native and
armv7l hardware with libgcc_s. It does not cover aarch64, LLVM libunwind,
concurrent cancellation, or mixed-runtime frame traversal.

中文说明：修复外来强制展开重抛状态丢失，并修复 ARM EHABI 将捕获
handler 误登记为 cleanup 的问题。两处必须作为同一系列应用。
---
 libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp   |  5 ++++-
 libcxxabi/src/cxa_personality.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp b/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp
index 5d7edae697d6..0a346f344b66 100644
--- a/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp
+++ b/libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp
@@ -648,7 +648,10 @@ void __cxa_rethrow() {
 #ifdef __USING_SJLJ_EXCEPTIONS__
     _Unwind_SjLj_RaiseException(&exception_header->unwindHeader);
 #else
-    _Unwind_RaiseException(&exception_header->unwindHeader);
+    if (native_exception)
+        _Unwind_RaiseException(&exception_header->unwindHeader);
+    else
+        _Unwind_Resume_or_Rethrow(&exception_header->unwindHeader);
 #endif
 
     //  If we get here, some kind of unwinding error has occurred.
diff --git a/libcxxabi/src/cxa_personality.cpp b/libcxxabi/src/cxa_personality.cpp
index 28208194edb3..3fd12fce9a16 100644
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: R51 Evidence <r51@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 20:20:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] libc++abi: expose GNU forced-unwind marker type
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GNU C++ code protects pthread cancellation with a handler for
__cxxabiv1::__forced_unwind, but libc++abi does not expose or map that marker.
Define the same abstract class shape used by libstdc++, with an out-of-line
virtual destructor so libc++abi owns one exported strong typeinfo definition.
Map a forced foreign exception to this type during personality matching.

This extension depends on the Layer A forced-unwind rethrow and ARM EHABI
handler fixes, at least on armv7l, because the matched handler rethrows the
foreign exception. Validation covers x86_64 native and armv7l hardware with
libgcc_s. It does not cover aarch64, LLVM libunwind, concurrent cancellation,
or mixed-runtime frame traversal.

中文说明：移植 GNU 强制展开标记类型及 personality 映射；采用抽象类
和库内 key function，保证消费者引用 libc++abi 中唯一的强 typeinfo。
该扩展在 armv7l 上依赖层 A。
---
 libcxxabi/include/cxxabi.h        |  8 ++++++++
 libcxxabi/src/cxa_exception.cpp   |  2 ++
 libcxxabi/src/cxa_personality.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 27 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libcxxabi/include/cxxabi.h b/libcxxabi/include/cxxabi.h
index 9ea93680f62e..da75b45c84fe 100644
--- a/libcxxabi/include/cxxabi.h
+++ b/libcxxabi/include/cxxabi.h
@@ -37,6 +37,14 @@ class type_info; // forward declaration
 // runtime routines use C calling conventions, but are in __cxxabiv1 namespace
 namespace __cxxabiv1 {
 
+// An out-of-line key function makes the runtime library own the unique
+// exported typeinfo definition. Keep the libstdc++ abstract class shape so
+// this marker can only be caught by reference.
+class _LIBCXXABI_TYPE_VIS __forced_unwind {
+  virtual ~__forced_unwind();
+  virtual void __pure_dummy() = 0;
+};
+
 struct __cxa_exception;
 
 extern "C"  {
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NOT_AVAILABLE <not-available@invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:59:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] libcxx: preserve forced unwind in consumer-instantiated
 handlers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Catch-all handlers in consumer-instantiated iostream, future, and string
paths intercept pthread cancellation's foreign forced unwind.  Preserve the
stream state updates and future state-machine obligations, then rethrow the
GNU ABI marker before the generic handlers can consume it.

Keep deferred work retryable after cancellation.  For async results, split
result construction from readiness publication so cancellation in the
pre-publication window atomically publishes broken_promise.  Reference
results use the same protocol without taking ownership of the referenced
object, and value-result destruction runs after releasing the shared-state
mutex.

The twenty guarded sites are delivered in this header batch because their
code may be instantiated into consumers under the supported build modes.
This change depends on the libc++abi forced-unwind marker and unwind fixes.

中文说明：
为消费者侧可能实例化的 iostream、future 与 string 共二十处站点补齐
强制展开防护；保留原状态更新后重抛取消展开。deferred 取消后恢复为
可重试；async 在发布前窗口原子完成为 broken_promise，引用结果不取得
对象所有权，值对象析构移到共享状态锁外。

Validation covers x86_64 and armv7l cancellation paths, async reference
results, concurrent waiters, stream state assertions, and normal exception
propagation.  Other architectures, LTO variants outside the audited set,
mixed runtimes, and dynamic loading boundaries are not covered.
---
 libcxx/include/__ostream/basic_ostream.h |   3 +
 libcxx/include/future                    | 142 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 libcxx/include/istream                   |  37 ++++++
 libcxx/include/string                    |   3 +
 libcxx/src/future.cpp                    |  10 +-
 5 files changed, 190 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libcxx/include/__ostream/basic_ostream.h b/libcxx/include/__ostream/basic_ostream.h
index 62770be72f98..67b9586cbc7c 100644
--- a/libcxx/include/__ostream/basic_ostream.h
+++ b/libcxx/include/__ostream/basic_ostream.h
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: He Fangyu <fangyu.he@samsung.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 20:52:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] libcxx: preserve forced unwind in library-delivered
 handlers
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Catch-all handlers in explicitly instantiated iostream paths consume foreign
forced unwind and can turn pthread cancellation into process termination.
Add typed handlers at the thirty sites whose implementation is delivered by
the shared libc++ library, preserving stream state before rethrowing.

For the badbit and failbit aggregation helpers, classify and rethrow while
the nested handler remains active; a later bare rethrow has no active
exception for foreign exception paths.  Streambuf extraction commits its
state with the non-throwing setter before rethrowing so an exception mask
cannot replace the forced unwind.

This library batch is separate from consumer-instantiated header sites and
depends on the libc++abi forced-unwind marker and unwind fixes.

中文说明：
为由 libc++ 动态库交付的三十处 iostream 站点补齐强制展开防护。
badbit/failbit 汇聚函数在活动 handler 内完成条件重抛，streambuf
提取路径以不抛异常的接口先提交状态位，再继续传播取消展开。

Validation covers x86_64 and armv7l cancellation paths, library-only
replacement, stream exception masks, state-bit assertions, and normal I/O
failure behavior.  Other architectures, unaudited LTO modes, mixed runtimes,
and dynamic loading boundaries are not covered.
---
 libcxx/include/istream | 63 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libcxx/src/ios.cpp     | 17 ++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libcxx/include/istream b/libcxx/include/istream
index fcf0452db691..c39dce589fa0 100644
--- a/libcxx/include/istream
+++ b/libcxx/include/istream
@@ -658,6 +658,12 @@ basic_istream<_CharT, _Traits>::operator>>(basic_streambuf<char_type, traits_typ
         if (__gc_ == 0)
           __state |= ios_base::failbit;
 #    if _LIBCPP_HAS_EXCEPTIONS
+      } catch (const __cxxabiv1::__forced_unwind&) {
+        __state |= ios_base::badbit;
+        if (__gc_ == 0)
